IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc25-remediation-approval.l4 -- Part XXII.1 Remediation Agreements of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: sections 715.36 to 715.43
-- (informing victims, court approval, the stay, variation, termination, recommencement, completion, the deadline, publication, regulations).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source and result conventions are those stated at the head of ccc25-remediation-negotiation.l4 (JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the text says no
-- in its own words; NOTHING where the text does not answer, including a grant named "may" whose "if" gate fails: the coordinator's ruling of 2026-11-12, one fork line per site in NOTES.md).
-- Dates are `Date day month year`. A period keeps the text's unit: "one year after" is `add years`, which clamps 29 February to 28 February.

§ `Section 715.36 -- Duty to inform victims`

-- 715.36 (1) After an organization has accepted the offer to negotiate according to the terms of the notice referred to in section 715.33, the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform any victim,
-- or any third party that is acting on the victim's behalf, that a remediation agreement may be entered into. "After" is a "when"-kind gate: before the offer is accepted the duty has not arisen (JUST FALSE).
-- src:14954 | 715.36 (1) After an organization has accepted the offer to negotiate according to the terms of the notice referred to in section 715.33, the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform any victim, or any third party that is acting on the victim’s behalf, that a remediation agreement may be entered into.
@ref s 715.36(1) (src:14954-14954)
GIVEN `an organization has accepted the offer to negotiate according to the terms of the notice referred to in section 715.33` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.36(1) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform any victim, or any third party acting on the victim’s behalf, that a remediation agreement may be entered into` MEANS
    IF `an organization has accepted the offer to negotiate according to the terms of the notice referred to in section 715.33`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After an organization has accepted the offer to negotiate according to the terms of the notice referred to in section 715.33"

-- 715.36 (2) The duty to inform any victim is to be construed and applied in a manner that is reasonable in the circumstances and not likely to interfere with the proper administration of justice,
-- including by causing interference with prosecutorial discretion or compromising, hindering or causing excessive delay to the negotiation of an agreement or its conclusion.
-- A rule of reading over a small typed representation of a manner of applying the duty. The "including by" examples are instances of interference, so any one of them is interference.
-- src:14956 | (2) The duty to inform any victim is to be construed and applied in a manner that is reasonable in the circumstances and not likely to interfere with the proper administration of justice, including by causing interference with prosecutorial discretion or compromising, hindering or causing excessive delay to the negotiation of an agreement or its conclusion.
@ref s 715.36(2) (src:14956-14956)
DECLARE `s 715.36(2) a manner of applying the duty to inform any victim` HAS
    `it is reasonable in the circumstances`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is likely to interfere with the proper administration of justice`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is likely to cause interference with prosecutorial discretion`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is likely to compromise the negotiation of an agreement or its conclusion`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is likely to hinder the negotiation of an agreement or its conclusion`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is likely to cause excessive delay to the negotiation of an agreement or its conclusion`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 715.36(2) (src:14956-14956)
GIVEN manner IS A `s 715.36(2) a manner of applying the duty to inform any victim`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.36(2) the duty to inform any victim is to be construed and applied in that manner` MEANS
    IF     manner's `it is reasonable in the circumstances`
       AND (NOT (    manner's `it is likely to interfere with the proper administration of justice`
                  OR manner's `it is likely to cause interference with prosecutorial discretion`
                  OR manner's `it is likely to compromise the negotiation of an agreement or its conclusion`
                  OR manner's `it is likely to hinder the negotiation of an agreement or its conclusion`
                  OR manner's `it is likely to cause excessive delay to the negotiation of an agreement or its conclusion`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be construed and applied in a manner that is reasonable in the circumstances and not likely to interfere with the proper administration of justice"

-- 715.36 (3) If the prosecutor elects not to inform a victim or third party under subsection (1), they must provide the court, when applying for approval of the agreement,
-- with a statement of the reasons why it was not appropriate to do so in the circumstances. A duty with an "if" (fork F8: a duty whose "if" is unmet).
-- src:14958 | (3) If the prosecutor elects not to inform a victim or third party under subsection (1), they must provide the court, when applying for approval of the agreement, with a statement of the reasons why it was not appropriate to do so in the circumstances.
@ref s 715.36(3) (src:14958-14958)
GIVEN `the prosecutor elects not to inform a victim or third party under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.36(3) the prosecutor must provide the court with a statement of the reasons why it was not appropriate to inform` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor elects not to inform a victim or third party under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the prosecutor elects not to inform a victim or third party under subsection (1)"

§ `Section 715.37 -- Application for court approval`

-- 715.37 (1) When the prosecutor and the organization have agreed to the terms of a remediation agreement, the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for an order approving the agreement.
-- src:14960 | 715.37 (1) When the prosecutor and the organization have agreed to the terms of a remediation agreement, the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for an order approving the agreement.
@ref s 715.37(1) (src:14960-14960)
GIVEN `the prosecutor and the organization have agreed to the terms of a remediation agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.37(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for an order approving the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor and the organization have agreed to the terms of a remediation agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the prosecutor and the organization have agreed to the terms of a remediation agreement"

-- 715.37 (2) The coming into force of the agreement is subject to the approval of the court. The function asks whether that condition has been met; it does not say that the agreement is in force.
-- src:14962 | (2) The coming into force of the agreement is subject to the approval of the court.
@ref s 715.37(2) (src:14962-14962)
GIVEN `the court has approved the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.37(2) the court’s approval, to which the coming into force of the agreement is subject, has been given` MEANS
    IF `the court has approved the agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is subject to the approval of the court"

-- 715.37 (3) To determine whether to approve the agreement, the court hearing an application must consider (a) any reparations, statement and other measure referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(g);
-- (b) any statement made by the prosecutor under subsection 715.36(3); (c) any victim or community impact statement presented to the court; and (d) any victim surcharge referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(h).
-- src:14964 | (3) To determine whether to approve the agreement, the court hearing an application must consider
-- src:14965 | (a) any reparations, statement and other measure referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(g);
