-- 715.37 (5) For the purpose of paragraph 715.34(1)(h), the amount of the victim surcharge is 30% of any penalty referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(f), or any other percentage that the prosecutor deems appropriate in the circumstances,
-- and is payable to the treasurer of the province in which the application for approval referred to in section 715.37 is made. A sum in dollars. The other percentage is the prosecutor's judgment: an input (a plain number of percent), never guessed.
-- The surcharge is "for the purpose of paragraph 715.34(1)(h)", which does not require one for an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act: for such an offence the subsection is NOT COVERED.
-- src:14975 | (5) For the purpose of paragraph 715.34(1)(h), the amount of the victim surcharge is 30% of any penalty referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(f), or any other percentage that the prosecutor deems appropriate in the circumstances, and is payable to the treasurer of the province in which the application for approval referred to in section 715.37 is made.
@ref s 715.37(5) (src:14975-14975)
GIVEN penalty IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage that the prosecutor deems appropriate in the circumstances, if the prosecutor deems another percentage appropriate` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the offence is an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 715.37(5) the amount of the victim surcharge in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the offence is an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of paragraph 715.34(1)(h)"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the percentage that the prosecutor deems appropriate in the circumstances, if the prosecutor deems another percentage appropriate`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (penalty TIMES 30%)
         WHEN JUST percentage THEN JUST (penalty TIMES (percentage DIVIDED BY 100))

@ref s 715.37(5) (src:14975-14975)
GIVEN `the application for approval is made in a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.37(5) the victim surcharge is payable to the treasurer of the province in which the application for approval is made` MEANS
    IF `the application for approval is made in a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payable to the treasurer of the province in which the application for approval referred to in section 715.37 is made"

