§ `Section 715.38 -- Variation order`

-- 715.38 On application by the prosecutor, the court must, by order, approve any modification to a remediation agreement if the court is satisfied that the agreement continues to meet the conditions set out in subsection 715.37(6).
-- On approval, the modification is deemed to form part of the agreement. The conditions are those of 715.37(6): the three inputs are the court's satisfaction, as there.
-- src:14988 | 715.38 On application by the prosecutor, the court must, by order, approve any modification to a remediation agreement if the court is satisfied that the agreement continues to meet the conditions set out in subsection 715.37(6). On approval, the modification is deemed to form part of the agreement.
@ref s 715.38 (src:14988-14988)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has applied for approval of the modification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the organization is charged with an offence to which the agreement applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the agreement is in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the terms of the agreement are fair, reasonable and proportionate to the gravity of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.38 the court must, by order, approve the modification to the remediation agreement` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prosecutor has applied for approval of the modification`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by the prosecutor"
    ELSE `s 715.37(6) the court must, by order, approve the agreement` `the court is satisfied that the organization is charged with an offence to which the agreement applies` `the court is satisfied that the agreement is in the public interest` `the court is satisfied that the terms of the agreement are fair, reasonable and proportionate to the gravity of the offence`   -- the conditions "set out in subsection 715.37(6)": JUST TRUE, or the text's "if it is satisfied" no

@ref s 715.38 (src:14988-14988)
GIVEN `the court has approved the modification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.38 the modification is deemed to form part of the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the court has approved the modification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On approval, the modification is deemed to form part of the agreement"

§ `Section 715.39 -- Termination order`

-- 715.39 (1) On application by the prosecutor, the court must, by order, terminate the agreement if it is satisfied that the organization has breached a term of the agreement.
-- src:14990 | 715.39 (1) On application by the prosecutor, the court must, by order, terminate the agreement if it is satisfied that the organization has breached a term of the agreement.
@ref s 715.39(1) (src:14990-14990)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has applied for an order terminating the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the organization has breached a term of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.39(1) the court must, by order, terminate the agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the prosecutor has applied for an order terminating the agreement` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by the prosecutor"
        IF NOT `the court is satisfied that the organization has breached a term of the agreement` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is satisfied that the organization has breached a term of the agreement"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 715.39 (2) As soon as the order is made, proceedings stayed in accordance with subsection 715.37(7) may be recommenced, without a new information or a new indictment, as the case may be,
-- by the prosecutor giving notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court in which the stay of the proceedings was entered. A grant ("may") with an "as soon as" ("upon") gate: listed, answer JUST FALSE (fork F10).
-- src:14992 | (2) As soon as the order is made, proceedings stayed in accordance with subsection 715.37(7) may be recommenced, without a new information or a new indictment, as the case may be, by the prosecutor giving notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court in which the stay of the proceedings was entered.
@ref s 715.39(2) (src:14992-14992)
GIVEN `an order terminating the agreement has been made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings were stayed in accordance with subsection 715.37(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.39(2) the stayed proceedings may be recommenced without a new information or a new indictment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an order terminating the agreement has been made under subsection (1)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As soon as the order is made"
        IF NOT `the proceedings were stayed in accordance with subsection 715.37(7)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings stayed in accordance with subsection 715.37(7) may be recommenced"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 715.39 (3) If no notice is given within one year after the order is made under subsection (1), or before the expiry of the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced, whichever is earlier,
-- the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced. The last day for notice is the earlier of the first anniversary of the order (the one-year period "after" the day of the order ends on the same date a year on:
-- fork F11) and the day the time for commencing the proceedings expires (an input: the text points outside the Act for that time).
-- src:14994 | (3) If no notice is given within one year after the order is made under subsection (1), or before the expiry of the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced, whichever is earlier, the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced.
@ref s 715.39(3) (src:14994-14994)
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 715.39(3) the last day on which notice of recommencement can be given to the clerk` MEANS
    IF `the first anniversary of the order` AT MOST `the day on which the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires`
    THEN `the first anniversary of the order`
    ELSE `the day on which the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires`
    WHERE
        `the first anniversary of the order` MEANS `add years` `the day on which the order is made under subsection (1)` 1

@ref s 715.39(3) (src:14994-14994)
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires` IS A DATE
      `the day on which notice of recommencement was given to the clerk, if it has been given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.39(3) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which notice of recommencement was given to the clerk, if it has been given`
    WHEN JUST given THEN
        IF given AT MOST `the last day for notice`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no notice is given within one year after the order is made under subsection (1)"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the last day for notice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no notice is given within one year after the order is made under subsection (1)" (the period has not yet run out: fork F11)
    WHERE
        `the last day for notice` MEANS `s 715.39(3) the last day on which notice of recommencement can be given to the clerk` `the day on which the order is made under subsection (1)` `the day on which the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires`

§ `Section 715.4 -- Order declaring successful completion`

-- 715.4 (1) On application by the prosecutor, the court must, by order, declare that the terms of the agreement were met if it is satisfied that the organization has complied with the agreement.
-- src:14996 | 715.4 (1) On application by the prosecutor, the court must, by order, declare that the terms of the agreement were met if it is satisfied that the organization has complied with the agreement.
@ref s 715.4(1) (src:14996-14996)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has applied for an order declaring that the terms of the agreement were met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the organization has complied with the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.4(1) the court must, by order, declare that the terms of the agreement were met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the prosecutor has applied for an order declaring that the terms of the agreement were met` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by the prosecutor"
        IF NOT `the court is satisfied that the organization has complied with the agreement` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is satisfied that the organization has complied with the agreement"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 715.4 (2) The order stays the proceedings against the organization for any offence to which the agreement applies, the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced and no other proceedings may be initiated
-- against the organization for the same offence. Three effects of the one order.
-- src:14998 | (2) The order stays the proceedings against the organization for any offence to which the agreement applies, the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced and no other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence.
@ref s 715.4(2) (src:14998-14998)
DECLARE `s 715.4(2) the effect of the order` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.4(2) the order stays the proceedings against the organization for any offence to which the agreement applies`
    `s 715.4(2) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced`
    `s 715.4(2) no other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence`

@ref s 715.4(2) (src:14998-14998)
GIVEN effect IS A `s 715.4(2) the effect of the order`
      `an order has been made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is one to which the agreement applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.4(2) the order has the effect` MEANS
    IF `an order has been made under subsection (1)` AND `the offence is one to which the agreement applies`
    THEN CONSIDER effect
         WHEN `s 715.4(2) the order stays the proceedings against the organization for any offence to which the agreement applies` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.4(2) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.4(2) no other proceedings may be initiated against the organization for the same offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The order stays the proceedings against the organization for any offence to which the agreement applies"

§ `Section 715.41 -- Deadline`

-- 715.41 (1) The prosecutor must, as soon as practicable after the deadline referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(p), apply to the court in writing for a variation order under section 715.38, including to extend the deadline,
-- an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39 or an order under section 715.4 declaring that its terms were met and the court may issue any of these orders as it deems appropriate.
-- src:15000 | 715.41 (1) The prosecutor must, as soon as practicable after the deadline referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(p), apply to the court in writing for a variation order under section 715.38, including to extend the deadline, an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39 or an order under section 715.4 declaring that its terms were met and the court may issue any of these orders as it deems appropriate.
@ref s 715.41(1) (src:15000-15000)
DECLARE `s 715.41(1) the order applied for` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.41(1) a variation order under section 715.38, including to extend the deadline`
    `s 715.41(1) an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39`
    `s 715.41(1) an order under section 715.4 declaring that its terms were met`
    `s 715.41(1) an order that none of those names`

@ref s 715.41(1) (src:15000-15000)
GIVEN `the deadline referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(p) has passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `s 715.41(1) the order applied for`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.41(1) the prosecutor must apply to the court in writing for the order` MEANS
    IF NOT `the deadline referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(p) has passed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as practicable after the deadline referred to in paragraph 715.34(1)(p)"
    ELSE CONSIDER order
         WHEN `s 715.41(1) a variation order under section 715.38, including to extend the deadline` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.41(1) an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.41(1) an order under section 715.4 declaring that its terms were met` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.41(1) an order that none of those names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to the court in writing for a variation order under section 715.38, including to extend the deadline, an order terminating the agreement under section 715.39 or an order under section 715.4"

@ref s 715.41(1) (src:15000-15000)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has applied for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `s 715.41(1) the order applied for`
      `the court deems it appropriate to issue the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.41(1) the court may issue the order as it deems appropriate` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor has applied for the order` AND `the court deems it appropriate to issue the order` AND (NOT (order EQUALS `s 715.41(1) an order that none of those names`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may issue any of these orders as it deems appropriate"

-- 715.41 (2) The agreement is deemed to remain in force until a court issues an order terminating it or declaring that its terms were met. An "until" bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05): TRUE before the order, JUST FALSE after it.
-- src:15002 | (2) The agreement is deemed to remain in force until a court issues an order terminating it or declaring that its terms were met.
@ref s 715.41(2) (src:15002-15002)
GIVEN `the agreement has come into force with the approval of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has issued an order terminating the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has issued an order declaring that its terms were met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.41(2) the agreement is deemed to remain in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the agreement has come into force with the approval of the court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The agreement is deemed to remain in force"
        IF `a court has issued an order terminating the agreement` OR `a court has issued an order declaring that its terms were met` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until a court issues an order terminating it or declaring that its terms were met"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 715.42 -- Publication`

-- 715.42 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the following must be published by the court as soon as practicable: (a) the remediation agreement approved by the court; (b) an order made under any of sections 715.37 to 715.41 and the reasons
-- for that order or the reasons for the decision not to make that order; and (c) a decision made under subsection (2) or (5) and the reasons for that decision.
-- src:15004 | 715.42 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the following must be published by the court as soon as practicable:
-- src:15005 | (a) the remediation agreement approved by the court;
-- src:15006 | (b) an order made under any of sections 715.37 to 715.41 and the reasons for that order or the reasons for the decision not to make that order; and
-- src:15007 | (c) a decision made under subsection (2) or (5) and the reasons for that decision.
@ref s 715.42(1) (src:15004-15007)
DECLARE `s 715.42(1) the item` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.42(1)(a) the remediation agreement approved by the court`
    `s 715.42(1)(b) an order made under any of sections 715.37 to 715.41 and the reasons for that order or the reasons for the decision not to make that order`
    `s 715.42(1)(c) a decision made under subsection (2) or (5) and the reasons for that decision`
    `s 715.42(1) an item that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names`

@ref s 715.42(1) (src:15004-15007)
GIVEN item IS A `s 715.42(1) the item`
      `the court has decided under subsection (2) not to publish the item` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.42(1) the court must publish the item as soon as practicable` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 715.42(1)(a) the remediation agreement approved by the court` THEN `unless the court has decided not to publish`
    WHEN `s 715.42(1)(b) an order made under any of sections 715.37 to 715.41 and the reasons for that order or the reasons for the decision not to make that order` THEN `unless the court has decided not to publish`
    WHEN `s 715.42(1)(c) a decision made under subsection (2) or (5) and the reasons for that decision` THEN JUST TRUE   -- subsection (2) lets the court withhold only the agreement and the orders and reasons of paragraph (1)(b), so no decision under (2) displaces this item
    WHEN `s 715.42(1) an item that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following must be published by the court as soon as practicable"
    WHERE
        `unless the court has decided not to publish` MEANS
            IF `the court has decided under subsection (2) not to publish the item`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (2)"
            ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 715.42 (2) The court may decide not to publish the agreement or any order or reasons referred to in paragraph (1)(b), in whole or in part, if it is satisfied that the non-publication is necessary for the proper administration of justice.
-- A grant ("may") with an "if" gate: when the court is not satisfied the answer is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (fork F2). The decision of paragraph (1)(c) is outside the power.
-- src:15009 | (2) The court may decide not to publish the agreement or any order or reasons referred to in paragraph (1)(b), in whole or in part, if it is satisfied that the non-publication is necessary for the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 715.42(2) (src:15009-15009)
GIVEN item IS A `s 715.42(1) the item`
      `the court is satisfied that the non-publication is necessary for the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.42(2) the court may decide not to publish the item` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (item EQUALS `s 715.42(1)(c) a decision made under subsection (2) or (5) and the reasons for that decision`) OR (item EQUALS `s 715.42(1) an item that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the agreement or any order or reasons referred to in paragraph (1)(b)"
        IF `the court is satisfied that the non-publication is necessary for the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is satisfied that the non-publication is necessary for the proper administration of justice"

-- 715.42 (3) To decide whether the proper administration of justice requires making the decision referred to in subsection (2), the court must consider (a) society's interest in encouraging the reporting of offences ...;
-- (b) whether it is necessary to protect the identity of any victims ...; (c) the prevention of any adverse effect to any ongoing investigation or prosecution; (d) whether effective alternatives ... are available; (e) the salutary and deleterious effects ...; and (f) any other factor that the court considers relevant.
-- src:15011 | (3) To decide whether the proper administration of justice requires making the decision referred to in subsection (2), the court must consider
-- src:15012 | (a) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims in the criminal justice process;
-- src:15013 | (b) whether it is necessary to protect the identity of any victims, any person not engaged in the wrongdoing and any person who brought the wrongdoing to the attention of investigative authorities;
-- src:15014 | (c) the prevention of any adverse effect to any ongoing investigation or prosecution;
-- src:15015 | (d) whether effective alternatives to the decision referred to in subsection (2) are available in the circumstances;
-- src:15016 | (e) the salutary and deleterious effects of making the decision referred to in subsection (2); and
-- src:15017 | (f) any other factor that the court considers relevant.
@ref s 715.42(3) (src:15011-15017)
DECLARE `s 715.42(3) the factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.42(3)(a) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims in the criminal justice process`
    `s 715.42(3)(b) whether it is necessary to protect the identity of any victims, any person not engaged in the wrongdoing and any person who brought the wrongdoing to the attention of investigative authorities`
    `s 715.42(3)(c) the prevention of any adverse effect to any ongoing investigation or prosecution`
    `s 715.42(3)(d) whether effective alternatives to the decision referred to in subsection (2) are available in the circumstances`
    `s 715.42(3)(e) the salutary and deleterious effects of making the decision referred to in subsection (2)`
    `s 715.42(3)(f) any other factor that the court considers relevant`

@ref s 715.42(3) (src:15011-15017)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 715.42(3) the factor`
      `the court considers the factor relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.42(3) the court must consider the factor` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `s 715.42(3)(a) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims in the criminal justice process` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.42(3)(b) whether it is necessary to protect the identity of any victims, any person not engaged in the wrongdoing and any person who brought the wrongdoing to the attention of investigative authorities` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.42(3)(c) the prevention of any adverse effect to any ongoing investigation or prosecution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.42(3)(d) whether effective alternatives to the decision referred to in subsection (2) are available in the circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.42(3)(e) the salutary and deleterious effects of making the decision referred to in subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.42(3)(f) any other factor that the court considers relevant` THEN IF `the court considers the factor relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any other factor that the court considers relevant"

-- 715.42 (4) The court may make its decision subject to any conditions that it considers appropriate, including a condition related to the duration of non-publication.
-- src:15019 | (4) The court may make its decision subject to any conditions that it considers appropriate, including a condition related to the duration of non-publication.
@ref s 715.42(4) (src:15019-15019)
GIVEN `the court has made a decision under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers the condition appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.42(4) the court may make its decision subject to the condition` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a decision under subsection (2)` AND `the court considers the condition appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "its decision subject to any conditions that it considers appropriate"

-- 715.42 (5) On application by any person, the court must review the decision made under subsection (2) to determine whether non-publication continues to be necessary for the proper administration of justice.
-- If the court is satisfied that the non-publication is no longer necessary, it must publish the agreement, order or reasons, as the case may be, in whole or in part, as soon as practicable.
-- src:15021 | (5) On application by any person, the court must review the decision made under subsection (2) to determine whether the non-publication continues to be necessary for the proper administration of justice. If the court is satisfied that the non-publication is no longer necessary, it must publish the agreement, order or reasons, as the case may be, in whole or in part, as soon as practicable.
@ref s 715.42(5) (src:15021-15021)
GIVEN `any person has applied for a review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.42(5) the court must review the decision made under subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `any person has applied for a review` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by any person"
        IF NOT `the decision was made under subsection (2)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court must review the decision made under subsection (2)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 715.42(5) (src:15021-15021)
GIVEN `the court has reviewed the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the non-publication is no longer necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.42(5) the court must publish the agreement, order or reasons, in whole or in part, as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF `the court has reviewed the decision` AND `the court is satisfied that the non-publication is no longer necessary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court is satisfied that the non-publication is no longer necessary"

§ `Section 715.43 -- Regulations; amendment of schedule; deleting an offence`

-- 715.43 (1) On the recommendation of the Minister of Justice, the Governor in Council may make regulations generally for the purposes of carrying out this Part, including regulations respecting (a) the form of the remediation agreement;
-- and (b) the verification of compliance by an independent monitor, including (i) the qualifications for monitors, (ii) the process to select a monitor, (iii) the form and content of a conflict of interest notification, and (iv) reporting requirements.
-- (2) On the recommendation of the Minister of Justice, the Governor in Council may, by order, amend the schedule by adding or deleting any offence to which a remediation agreement may apply.
-- Regulation-making powers and the power to amend a schedule by order are machinery (coverage rows, inert, reason 2): they bind no one now, and the schedule as it stands is the answer of another part's range.
-- src:15023 | 715.43 (1) On the recommendation of the Minister of Justice, the Governor in Council may make regulations generally for the purposes of carrying out this Part, including regulations respecting
-- src:15024 | (a) the form of the remediation agreement; and
-- src:15025 | (b) the verification of compliance by an independent monitor, including
-- src:15026 | (i) the qualifications for monitors,
-- src:15027 | (ii) the process to select a monitor,
-- src:15028 | (iii) the form and content of a conflict of interest notification, and
-- src:15029 | (iv) reporting requirements.
-- src:15030 | Amendment of schedule
-- src:15031 | (2) On the recommendation of the Minister of Justice, the Governor in Council may, by order, amend the schedule by adding or deleting any offence to which a remediation agreement may apply.
@ref s 715.43(1) and (2) (src:15023-15031)
`s 715.43(1) and (2) the regulation-making and schedule-amending powers as the text states them` MEANS "the Governor in Council may make regulations generally for the purposes of carrying out this Part, and may amend the schedule by order"

-- 715.43 (3) If the Governor in Council orders the deletion of an offence from the schedule to this Part, this Part continues to apply to an organization alleged to have committed that offence
-- if a notice referred to in section 715.33 respecting that offence was sent to the organization before the day on which the order comes into force.
-- When no deletion has been ordered, or the organization is not alleged to have committed that offence, the subsection does not speak, so the answer is NOTHING (fork F29; the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "If" on the provision's own question).
-- src:15033 | (3) If the Governor in Council orders the deletion of an offence from the schedule to this Part, this Part continues to apply to an organization alleged to have committed that offence if a notice referred to in section 715.33 respecting that offence was sent to the organization before the day on which the order comes into force.
@ref s 715.43(3) (src:15033-15033)
GIVEN `the Governor in Council has ordered the deletion of the offence from the schedule to this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the organization is alleged to have committed that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice referred to in section 715.33 respecting that offence was sent to the organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the notice was sent` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the order comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.43(3) this Part continues to apply to the organization despite the deletion of the offence from the schedule` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Governor in Council has ordered the deletion of the offence from the schedule to this Part`) OR (NOT `the organization is alleged to have committed that offence`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Governor in Council orders the deletion of an offence from the schedule to this Part, this Part continues to apply to an organization alleged to have committed that offence"
        IF `a notice referred to in section 715.33 respecting that offence was sent to the organization` AND `the day on which the notice was sent` LESS THAN `the day on which the order comes into force` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a notice referred to in section 715.33 respecting that offence was sent to the organization before the day on which the order comes into force"

§ `Regulative rules of sections 715.36 to 715.42 (the same duties and permissions, run with #TRACE in the tests file)`

-- Each rule below is the duty, permission or bar ONCE IT HAS ARISEN, and carries no gate. The conditions under which it arises ("if", "where", "when", "after") are tested by the decision function of the same section, and the #TRACE runs in the tests file show what follows from doing or not doing the act, never whether the duty arose.

-- No deadline, consequence or remedy is added that the text does not state. The one number in this group is "immediately" in 715.37(7), read as WITHIN 0 (fork F9).
DECLARE `s 715.36 to 715.42 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.36(1) take reasonable steps to inform any victim or third party`
    `s 715.36(3) provide the court with a statement of reasons`
    `s 715.37(1) apply to the court in writing for an order approving the agreement`
    `s 715.37(3) consider the matters`
    `s 715.37(4)(a) consider the victim or community impact statement or other evidence concerning any victim`
    `s 715.37(4)(c) make reasonable efforts to provide a copy of the statement to the organization or counsel for the organization`
    `s 715.37(6) approve the agreement by order`
    `s 715.37(7) direct the clerk or other proper officer to make an entry on the record`
    `s 715.37(7) make the entry on the record that the proceedings are stayed`
    `s 715.38 approve the modification by order`
    `s 715.39(1) terminate the agreement by order`
    `s 715.39(2) give notice of the recommencement to the clerk of the court`
    `s 715.4(1) declare by order that the terms of the agreement were met`
    `s 715.41(1) apply to the court in writing for an order`
    `s 715.42(1) publish`
    `s 715.42(2) decide not to publish`
    `s 715.42(3) consider the factors`
    `s 715.42(5) review the decision made under subsection (2)`
    `s 715.42(5) publish after the review`

-- src:14954 | 715.36 (1) After an organization has accepted the offer to negotiate according to the terms of the notice referred to in section 715.33, the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform any victim, or any third party that is acting on the victim’s behalf, that a remediation agreement may be entered into.
@ref s 715.36(1) (src:14954-14954)
