`s 715.36(1) the prosecutor's duty to inform victims` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    MUST `s 715.36(1) take reasonable steps to inform any victim or third party`

-- src:14958 | (3) If the prosecutor elects not to inform a victim or third party under subsection (1), they must provide the court, when applying for approval of the agreement, with a statement of the reasons why it was not appropriate to do so in the circumstances.
@ref s 715.36(3) (src:14958-14958)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 715.36 to 715.42 act`
